ugh  i guess everything in black clover to  date also astor gets a new toy or a new  form of toyota is it a new sword or is  it like  i don't know yet this cloverclad sword  that can definitely apparently break the  reincarnation spell which he was  previously unable to do  although my first thought is why didn't  you break the spell on yuno right then  and there  there is still an elf on that shelf of a  boy and i think that that could be a  grand threat in the future and i do get  that he's more powerful in this form  i think i don't actually know that but  you know is a boss anyway so why not  rid ourselves of this elvish compromise  in any case we didn't do that but it's a  wonderful part of the story to read  regardless after which we arrive at a  slightly more intense confrontation with  luck and there are lots of things i like  about this one of which is that we get  to call back to the whole flashback with  his mother and that pays off so nicely  because we've now spent a ton of time  with him it's much easier to feel the  whole luck is our friend thing when  asked her says it rather than when it  originally happened way back in the  second arc where astor said it like  five minutes after meeting lock but  there was also this really heartwarming  panel of his mother looking on as luck  tells her that he has to go back and  that was oh that was very sweet a nice  way to expand his story and even  potentially bring some closure to the  character because his mother looks  incredibly proud of him and seemingly  for all of the right reasons this time  also my favorite spell in the series  destiny cat got to be featured a bit  more and it came equipped with the  limitations i was seeking from that  whole witch arc  as it turns out it is indeed a massive  mana drain on vanessa as it should be  but it's still an incredibly ridiculous  utility kitty which when implemented as  part of a team is absolutely invaluable  i love it it was also very interesting  in exactly 