ter experiencing those pages i do  actually feel for his situation quite a  bit more it's a massive moral quandary  like what are you supposed to do when  you're infinitely loyal to one party  and profoundly empathize with another so  it was quite sad to hear that he had  passed into what i think was called  endlessly but at the same time there's a  lot of room to bring him back as well  because after the discovery of astor's  reincarnation breaker it's feeling more  and more like we'll just take these  people back one by one  and in the end if not licked is defeated  then surely that body just returns to  william  i think no i don't know i actually don't  know at all i have no idea however it  was rather bittersweet to learn that  even this super evil not like delph did  consider william to be a true friend  their only human friend which once again  opens up the potential gates of empathy  for even this seemingly  unrecoverable character in reincarnation  in some form or another continues to be  a very strong theme of this arc even  without elvish madness because rather  sally and the other one well they also  managed to bring their souls back into  their bodies more specifically because  of rades which i was not expecting at  all i thought they were just done and  dusted goodbye weird ass trio but  instead it's like hello again weird ass  trio and i dare say it's nice to see  them again  because now that they're temporary  allies they're actually kind of fun to  be around radas in particular seems to  do very well with comic elements  alongside asda and i do  have a soft spot for antagonist flipping  sides it's also good to have another  spatial magic user on this side in  finral stead because that seems pretty  damn essential the more i read of the  series the more i get the impression  that spatial magic is wildly overpowered  and probably the most useful utility one  can really have as part of a team with  that said i am getting a bit worried  that nobody in this arc seems to be  capable of dying i mean i think there  are actually a few nobles who are sorted  but nobody cares about them we're  talking about named characters which i  suppose make sense it's the  reincarnation  arc not the kill everyone arc but it  makes me more nervous that tarbata is  going to go back on the whole wizard  king killing idea that doesn't matter  for now though because let's talk about  noel holy crap this situation is a huge  part of why i had to stop because her  involvement is probably my favorite part  of the circle as far it was great to see  her fight for and alongside her siblings  specifically nozzle who had some  fantastic words  specifically stuff like not you noel  you're a royal you're coming with me to  defend the castle and also the fact that  he ended up apologizing to her which is  that's pretty well and to top it all off  noelle is now  incredible having conjured that water  valkyrie armor which while she does not  possess her mother's magic finity still  evokes her almost entirely and turns  noelle into a fully fledged combatant  with this spell surely she does not sit  on the sidelines anymore and only get  tapped to support and i also very much  enjoyed the explanation for how noel can  access something like this which i think  was something along the lines of well  royals are born with phenomenal magic  but they never bother to train it  meanwhile commoners are born with feeble  magic but train heavily to make it  potent and then there's noel who was  born with absurd magic  and trained it thus catapulting her into  a whole new sphere of magical  shenanigany it shows her hard work  paying off and this situation was also  perfectly sculpted to noel because their  elvish opponent was using a brand of  magic that disturbs the minor control of  others which is very interesting because  that's  kind of noel's entire problem all her  life she has been operating under these  conditions of terrible  terrible mana control so her siblings  got a taste of what it was like to be  noel and they were  completely useless for the most part  meanwhile noel who is very much  experienced under these conditions rose  to the occasions and in a stroke of  brilliance even concocted a plan to  drown a fool and it didn't work in the  end but it was still a fantastic idea  and while the whole thing was just  glorious it actually pairs very well  alongside astor and yuno's return to  their village in the same way that they  got to go home and protect their roots  noel also experienced something of a  homecoming and stood up to protect the  house of silva which i guess is probably  just referred to as house silver and  that idea of protecting home is  obviously a huge motif in this section  because everyone's place of safety is  under attack  and while it's not quite as potent as  noel's seen we do have a similar  situation happening with the crimson  lions and leopold defending his squad  from an  elf which does lead us to the fantastic  return of fuego leon i have been waiting  for this man to show up for an awfully  long time now and he did not disappoint  in fact he's better than ever because he  has taken command of fauna's  well one of the fauna's salamander  spirits which yeah he is at this point  in time the absolutely perfect vessel  for that and i cannot wait to see him  destroy some fools  on behalf of his sister meanwhile  everywhere else everyone is playing out  their own fated individual conflicts  like yami facing off against charlotte  which doesn't play out to a conclusion  also finral versus langris but there's a  wide breadth of conflict to play with  which only works so well because tarbata  has slowly but surely built up these  little relationships which sometimes yes  that building is clunky and weird and  doesn't quite fit into the arc specific  situations but it does pay off in  something like this because we could  have had a much more standard shonen  approach where certain protagonists each  need to face off against a random enemy  where you don't necessarily care but i  find myself carrying quite a bit here  because even if the elves have taken  over certain bodies that character  dynamic is still sort of in play i mean  even the purple orca captain  dude got some time to himself and i  honestly never thought we'd see him  again so all of these characters are  beginning to pay off in some way or  another and that is exciting because we  still have a fair few more to go this  arc is anything but over and right now  i'm just being taunted with the thought  of one of the last things i've currently  seen which was the opening of what i  think was called the shadow palace a  very ominous dimensional construct  hidden or sealed within the clover  kingdom which also delivers our first  calamity scale event in black clover  which is that seemingly the idea is to  put a stone in a thing and sacrifice all  of the human souls in elf commented  bodies and that's  that's pretty bad but also fun because  it does at least artificially raise the  stakes of the ark to a level we've not  previously seen with black clover and  look it's a very one piece standard  device actually in every mega rock there  is always this  localized apocalypse that we need to  stop in addition to actually defeating  the ultimate antagonist  and they're great because they create  chaos and also they give characters who  have no business fighting the main  antagonist something to in the meantime  you know they're charged with stopping  the catastrophe  but i suppose we'll see how things play  out in any case i'm pretty excited to  conclude the reincarnation arc which i  promise we will do  next week but that pretty much does it  for this blind review of part 2 of the  reincarnation arc and what do you guys  think please do leave your thoughts in  the comments below or even join my  discord server and if you're keen for  small black clover content then please  to go and check out some of my other  videos or even subscribe to the channel  for very maybe black clover goodness  delivered straight into your youtube  feed but for now this has been the new  world review and i'll see you next time

